<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Prestige & Willshaw (1975) & Brown et al. (2000) EphA/ephrin-A retinotectal chemoaffinity & synaptic competition (Danio rerio zebrafish / Mus musculus vertebrate retinotectal-retinocollicular projection)",
        "Prestige & Willshaw (1975) & Brown et al. (2000) EphA/ephrin-A retinotectal chemoaffinity & synaptic competition faithfully reproduces Danio rerio zebrafish / Mus musculus vertebrate retinotectal-retinocollicular projection morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 1976-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Danio rerio zebrafish / Mus musculus vertebrate retinotectal-retinocollicular projection specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 92.4/100, audit 2026-10-19-retinotectal-chemoaffinity-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1976-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity.py> ;
    schema:about "Danio rerio zebrafish / Mus musculus vertebrate retinotectal-retinocollicular projection" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Subcellular growth-cone filopodial actin polymerization or EphB/ephrin-B dorsoventral mediolateral axis guidance",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D synaptic weight matrix ODE dW_ij/dt with EphA/ephrin-A counter-gradients, Sinkhorn-Knopp Group II row/column homeostatic normalization, and cooperative kernel K_ret * W * K_tec across all 6 experimental regimes plus a 12x12 (Delta_R_EphA3, mu_comp) morphospace",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Automated CV segmentation of the 72 hpf Danio rerio larval retina confocal micrograph (concentric inner nuclear r=295 px and outer plexiform r=392 px rings, 60-bin radial fluorescence profile r=0.9897, and N=415 neural clusters across the nasal-temporal arc)",
        "reported_in_source: Brown et al. (2000) Cell 102:77-88 Isl2-EphA3 knock-in experiments showing relative EphA signaling bifurcates the retinocollicular projection into two non-overlapping maps in ki/ki homozygotes and a rostral-convergent split map in ki/+ heterozygotes",
        "reported_in_source: Prestige & Willshaw (1975) Proc. R. Soc. B 190:77-98 Group I (rigid affinity) vs Group II (relative synaptic resource competition) explaining half-tectum map compression (slope -0.50) and half-retina map expansion (slope -2.00)",
        "reported_in_source: Willshaw & von der Malsburg (1976) Proc. R. Soc. B 194:431-445 cooperative short-range neighborhood coupling sharpening retinotectal arbors",
        "transfer_boundary: Normalized 1D nasal-temporal retinal coordinate x in [0, 1] and rostral-caudal tectal/collicular coordinate y in [0, 1] coupled via the 40x40 synaptic weight matrix W_ij" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "9. Bioelectric V_mem & Attractors" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Target Polarity & Neural Maps" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Bistable V_mem / G_ij Threshold" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Pisces (Ichthyes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Danio" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/1976-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity.py; output: docs/media/retinotectal_chemoaffinity_comparison.png; organism: Danio rerio zebrafish / Mus musculus vertebrate retinotectal-retinocollicular projection; checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 291d0b05f4ef97593e7998ed422cf0c6840ddc0d18ee83dd5143a46bbb22b878; artifact_sha256: c1f0088ab7aec507c657c7913003673aef0829ca8f48a31826824e1aaa0c9a0b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/paper_citations.bib=aad29a956cd55dc1..., datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/retinotectal_chemoaffinity_reference.json=86046fcab644c7a3..., datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/scout_manifest.json=5ccb8a42580e5070..., datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/zebrafish_retinotectal_specimen.jpg=e16ecb3325a48823...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-retinotectal-chemoaffinity-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Prestige & Willshaw (1975) Proc. R. Soc. B 190:77-98 Group I (rigid affinity) vs Group II (relative synaptic resource competition) explaining half-tectum map compression (slope -0.50) and half-retina map expansion (slope -2.00) | Brown et al. (2000) Cell 102:77-88 Isl2-EphA3 knock-in experiments showing relative EphA signaling bifurcates the retinocollicular projection into two non-overlapping maps in ki/ki homozygotes and a rostral-convergent split map in ki/+ heterozygotes | Willshaw & von der Malsburg (1976) Proc. R. Soc. B 194:431-445 cooperative short-range neighborhood coupling sharpening retinotectal arbors; reconstructed_in_script: 2D synaptic weight matrix ODE dW_ij/dt with EphA/ephrin-A counter-gradients, Sinkhorn-Knopp Group II row/column homeostatic normalization, and cooperative kernel K_ret * W * K_tec across all 6 experimental regimes plus a 12x12 (Delta_R_EphA3, mu_comp) morphospace | Automated CV segmentation of the 72 hpf Danio rerio larval retina confocal micrograph (concentric inner nuclear r=295 px and outer plexiform r=392 px rings, 60-bin radial fluorescence profile r=0.9897, and N=415 neural clusters across the nasal-temporal arc); transfer_boundary: Normalized 1D nasal-temporal retinal coordinate x in [0, 1] and rostral-caudal tectal/collicular coordinate y in [0, 1] coupled via the 40x40 synaptic weight matrix W_ij; does_not_claim: Subcellular growth-cone filopodial actin polymerization or EphB/ephrin-B dorsoventral mediolateral axis guidance]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0092-8674(00)00012-X>,
