<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Prestige & Willshaw (1975) & Brown et al. (2000) EphA/ephrin-A retinotectal chemoaffinity & synaptic competition — MorphoEval overall 92.4/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `1976-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity.py` (92.4/100, up from 57.3/100 in Pass 1; +35.1 overall). The remediated script solves the 2D retinotectal synaptic weight matrix W_ij(t) ODE with Prestige-Willshaw Group II homeostatic row/column competition and cooperative neighborhood coupling across all 6 canonical experimental regimes: Wild-Type inverted mapping (`slope = -0.9976`, `r = -1.0000`), Brown et al. (2000) Isl2-EphA3/EphA3 homozygous `ki/ki` non-overlapping map duplication (`Delta_y = 0.5122`), Isl2-EphA3/+ heterozygous `ki/+` partial bifurcation (`Delta_y = 0.2785`), Prestige & Willshaw (1975) Group II caudal half-tectum compression (`slope = -0.4947` vs Group I nasal pileup), temporal half-retina 2x expansion (`slope = -1.9986`), and Ephrin-A2/A5 double-knockout scrambled control (`r = -0.0528`), paired with automated CV segmentation of the concentric retinal neural laminae (`r = 0.9897`, `N = 415` neural clusters) on the 72 hpf Danio rerio confocal specimen (`zebrafish_retinotectal_specimen.jpg`) and 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_086_retinotectal_chemoaffinity.lean`. Overall 92.4/100 (faithfulness 92.2, reproducibility 92.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 91, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 93. Output judged: docs/media/retinotectal_chemoaffinity_comparison.png: rendered output of 1976-willshaw-retinotectal-chemoaffinity.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 898070 B, 2227×1863 px, artifact_sha256 c1f0088ab7aec507c657c7913003673aef0829ca8f48a31826824e1aaa0c9a0b (sha256 c1f0088ab7aec507c657c7913003673aef0829ca8f48a31826824e1aaa0c9a0b), spec_fingerprint 291d0b05f4ef97593e7998ed422cf0c6840ddc0d18ee83dd5143a46bbb22b878. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 291d0b05f4ef97593e7998ed422cf0c6840ddc0d18ee83dd5143a46bbb22b878; artifact_sha256: c1f0088ab7aec507c657c7913003673aef0829ca8f48a31826824e1aaa0c9a0b; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/paper_citations.bib=aad29a956cd55dc1..., datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/retinotectal_chemoaffinity_reference.json=86046fcab644c7a3..., datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/scout_manifest.json=5ccb8a42580e5070..., datasets/retinotectal_chemoaffinity/zebrafish_retinotectal_specimen.jpg=e16ecb3325a48823...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-retinotectal-chemoaffinity-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Prestige & Willshaw (1975) Proc. R. Soc. B 190:77-98 Group I (rigid affinity) vs Group II (relative synaptic resource competition) explaining half-tectum map compression (slope -0.50) and half-retina map expansion (slope -2.00) | Brown et al. (2000) Cell 102:77-88 Isl2-EphA3 knock-in experiments showing relative EphA signaling bifurcates the retinocollicular projection into two non-overlapping maps in ki/ki homozygotes and a rostral-convergent split map in ki/+ heterozygotes | Willshaw & von der Malsburg (1976) Proc. R. Soc. B 194:431-445 cooperative short-range neighborhood coupling sharpening retinotectal arbors; reconstructed_in_script: 2D synaptic weight matrix ODE dW_ij/dt with EphA/ephrin-A counter-gradients, Sinkhorn-Knopp Group II row/column homeostatic normalization, and cooperative kernel K_ret * W * K_tec across all 6 experimental regimes plus a 12x12 (Delta_R_EphA3, mu_comp) morphospace | Automated CV segmentation of the 72 hpf Danio rerio larval retina confocal micrograph (concentric inner nuclear r=295 px and outer plexiform r=392 px rings, 60-bin radial fluorescence profile r=0.9897, and N=415 neural clusters across the nasal-temporal arc); transfer_boundary: Normalized 1D nasal-temporal retinal coordinate x in [0, 1] and rostral-caudal tectal/collicular coordinate y in [0, 1] coupled via the 40x40 synaptic weight matrix W_ij; does_not_claim: Subcellular growth-cone filopodial actin polymerization or EphB/ephrin-B dorsoventral mediolateral axis guidance." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple spontaneous retinal cholinergic wave correlations to the Willshaw-von der Malsburg cooperative kernel K_ret.",
        "remediation needed: Extend the 1D nasal-temporal / rostral-caudal W_ij matrix to a 4D retinotectal tensor incorporating orthogonal dorsoventral EphB/ephrin-B attractive signaling." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.24e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

